Release Date: 	3/6/2017
SVN Revision #:	10898
Agency:		GNM
Data Level:	Loan
Periods:	All
Data Field:	All

Update:
This release is preparision for GNMA model v2.00. Data update involves all five GNMA loan level tables:
	- Scale.GNM_loan
	- Scale.GNM_loanHist
	- Scale.GNM_loanEligbility
	- Scale.GNM_loanIncentive
	- Scale.GNM_loanBurnout
1. Loan Origination (Scale.GNM_loan)
	Based on v1.00 table, we did the following updates:
	a)  Add five additional variables to the table
	loanType
	loanPurposeType
	tpoType
	firstTimeHomeBuyerFlag
	reperformingStatus
b) Data Cleaning
	In order to fill in the Nulls, we used two approaches: Nearest-neighbor and Binning to find a most similar (or closest) record for each missing data point. We applied the filling algorithm for the following three variables:
	origFICO
	origLTV
	loanPurposeType
	The detailed algorithm can be found in the Google Doc:
	https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eawGJ_R24HpQkE_Ujej7HjkV-AdJLJBP-sFgDjYR5Kc/edit

2. Loan Hist 
	The loan hist table contents the monthly updated time series data for each loan. New updates for v2.00 release include:
	a) Add additional variables to scale.gnm_loan
	loanAge
	delMonths
	removalReasonType
	schamBalance
	b) Data Cleaning
	Fill in Null data points for the following variables:
	loanAge
	cltv
	schamBalance
	LoanAge will be calculated by origination date and current asof date;
	CLTV is estimated by HPI and OLTV, with the assumption of scheduled amortization;
	SchamBalance used calcScham as the primary source.

3. Loan Eligibility
	Followed the conventional v2.41 algorithm and applied them on GNMA loans. Only calculated the GNMA to conventional eligibility. GNMA to GNMA refi-eligibility will assign to be always eligible.

4. Loan Incentive
	Update the GNMA v1.0 incentive calculation to a similar calculation used in conventional v2.41 version.
	Included GNM to conventional incentive
	Incentive  = max(GNMA incentive, conventional incentive)
	Use different mortgage rate in GNMA to GNMA and GNMA to conventional incentive
	Included the incentive_eligible version as an additional variable. That is defined as the incentive for the case when it's available to refinance. (only apply to GNMA to conventional refi)
5. Loan Burnout
	Updated the burnout calculation from v1.0 to the most up to date v2.41 conventional algorithm.
	Use absolute incentive instead of relative incentive
	Count incentive only when the loan is eligible to refi (only apply to GNMA to conventional refi)
	Cap incentive at 200 bps


